1
00:02:27,500 --> 00:02:33,500
Doctor Who: Planet of the Dead is a science fiction, tv
movie, thriller film directed by James Strong.

2
00:04:55,000 --> 00:05:01,000
A meeting in a London bus with jewel thief Lady Christina takes a turn for the worse for the Doctor
when the bus takes a detour to a desert-like planet, where the deadly Swarm awaits.

3
00:07:22,500 --> 00:07:28,500
The Doctor, played by David Tennant.

4
00:09:50,000 --> 00:09:56,000
Christina, played by Michelle Ryan.

5
00:12:17,500 --> 00:12:23,500
Malcolm, played by Lee Evans.

6
00:14:45,000 --> 00:14:51,000
Capt Magambo, played by Noma Dumezweni.

7
00:17:12,500 --> 00:17:18,500
DI McMillan, played by Adam James.

8
00:19:40,000 --> 00:19:46,000
Sgt Dennison, played by Glenn Doherty.

9
00:22:07,500 --> 00:22:13,500
"Planet of the Dead" is the first of four special episodes of the British science fiction
television series Doctor Who broadcast between mid-2009 and early 2010.

10
00:24:35,000 --> 00:24:41,000
It was simultaneously broadcast on BBC One and BBC
HD on 11 April 2009 (Holy Saturday).

11
00:27:02,500 --> 00:27:08,500
The specials served as lead actor David Tennant's
final stories as the Tenth Doctor.

12
00:29:30,000 --> 00:29:36,000
He is joined in the episode by actress Michelle Ryan, who plays Lady
Christina de Souza, a one-off companion to the Doctor.

13
00:31:57,500 --> 00:32:03,500
The episode was written by Russell T Davies and Gareth Roberts, the
first co-writing credit since the show's revival in 2005.

14
00:34:25,000 --> 00:34:31,000
"Planet of the Dead" serves as the 200th story of Doctor Who.

15
00:36:52,500 --> 00:36:58,500
The episode depicts Christina fleeing the police from a museum robbery by boarding a bus that accidentally travels from London to
the desert planet of San Helios, trapping her, the Doctor, and several passengers on board the damaged vehicle.

16
00:39:20,000 --> 00:39:26,000
After the bus driver dies trying to return to Earth, the Unified Intelligence Taskforce, headed by Captain Erisa Magambo (Noma Dumezweni) and scientific
advisor Malcolm Taylor (Lee Evans), attempt to return the bus while preventing a race of metallic stingray aliens from posing a threat to Earth.

17
00:41:47,500 --> 00:41:53,500
At the end of the episode, one of the passengers delivers a warning to the Doctor that
"he will knock four times", foreshadowing the remaining three specials.

18
00:44:15,000 --> 00:44:21,000
"Planet of the Dead" was the first Doctor Who episode to be filmed in high definition, after a positive reaction to the visual
quality of spin-off series Torchwood and the financial viability of HDTV convinced the production team to switch formats.

19
00:46:42,500 --> 00:46:48,500
To ensure that the desert scenes looked as realistic as possible, the production team filmed in Dubai for three days,
sending several props, including a 1980 double-decker Bristol VR bus, to the United Arab Emirates for filming.

20
00:49:10,000 --> 00:49:16,000
After a shipping container unintentionally damaged the bus in Dubai, Davies
rewrote the script to explain the damage in the narrative.

21
00:51:37,500 --> 00:51:43,500
The audience gave the episode an Appreciation
Index of 88—considered "excellent."

22
00:54:05,000 --> 00:54:11,000
The film explores themes of sand, alien, tv special.

23
00:56:32,500 --> 00:56:38,500
The tone is mind_bending and thought_provoking and intense.
